      "observed": "On the CAN BUS sheets, the parts designated D9 and D10 are drawn as optocouplers (two LED inputs with light arrows and a phototransistor output, pins 'Input'/'Output'), placed in series between the CAN transceiver CANH/CANL lines (U11, U10) and the bus nets CAN0_P/CAN0_N and CAN1_P/CAN1_N that go to the M12 connectors J2/J13. No CDSOT23-SM712 / SM712 TVS diode array symbol appears anywhere on the CAN lines.",
      "expected": "The specification's component table states that D9 and D10 are 'CDSOT23-SM712 TVS diode arrays on CAN0_P/N, CAN1_P/N' for 'CAN bus transient/ESD protection', and that twistedfields-notes.txt lists 'TVS Diodes: SM712-TP or SM712-02HTG' as the intended part family. The intended design therefore has parallel TVS protection arrays on the CAN bus lines, not series optocouplers in the differential data path.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "D9, D10 — CDSOT23-SM712 TVS diode arrays on CAN0_P/N, CAN1_P/N | CAN bus transient/ESD protection | docs/twistedfields-notes.txt lists 'TVS Diodes: SM712-TP or SM712-02HTG' ... the netlist's CDSOT23-SM712 matches this documented choice."},
