      ],
      "impact": "The CAN0/CAN1 buses lose their specified transient/ESD protection, and the series optocouplers in the differential CAN path would attenuate/distort the CAN signaling, likely breaking reliable communication with the Odrive motor controllers on J2/J13.",
      "confidence": 0.5
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Most of the board matches the spec (16 MHz crystals on both MCP2515s, the four SN74LVC1G07 e-stop buffers U15/U22/U35/U36, the LTC4412+P-MOSFET USB OR-ing, the GLOBAL_EN switch path, Ethernet TVS arrays, and the isolated CAN transceivers). The one deviation I can read off the drawing is that the CAN-bus protection parts D9/D10 are implemented as series optocouplers instead of the parallel CDSOT23-SM712 TVS arrays the specification mandates, removing the intended CAN transient/ESD protection and altering the differential bus path."
}

